<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
Qualification Baseline Block (3D)

The opponent every commit must not lose to. Palette plastic (950 kg/m3, sliding
friction 0.25 — configs/rules/materials_store.yaml) in a box of half-extents
0.60 0.60 0.125, i.e. a 1.2 x 1.2 x 0.25 m slab:

    volume = 1.2 x 1.2 x 0.25 = 0.36 m3
    mass   = 0.36 x 950       = 342 kg

User decision 2026-09-16 (audit flag F-N11): the block is made of a palette
material like every other asset in the arena, and weighs roughly a third to a
half of the 800 kg mass cap, so shoving it off the ring is a real test of a
design. Plastic's low sliding friction lets the slab slide rather than grip, so
a bot that gets under it can still move it.

Nothing here is a hand-picked physics number:
  * mass= is the palette product above, baked so that any path composing this
    file raw weighs the same slab as qualification does.
  * contact settings are the environment's: composition runs both robot trees
    through normalize_robot_collision_settings, which owns condim (6),
    priority (2), solref, solimp, margin and gap.
  * sliding friction is NOT baked — the qualification path resolves it from the
    palette (0.25, via mjarena.core.qualification_block). A path that composes
    this file raw carries no friction of its own, so composition falls back to
    a sliding friction of 1.0 for it.

Has a freejoint for 3D physics but no actuators, so it just sits there until
pushed; its blue_ prefix exempts it from the inactivity rule.
-->
<mujoco model="stationary_block_3d">
  <compiler angle="radian"/>

  <asset>
    <!-- visual only; the physics of the same name comes from the palette -->
    <material name="plastic" rgba="0.95 0.95 0.95 1" specular="0.1" shininess="0.1"/>
  </asset>

  <default>
    <joint damping="0.0" armature="0.0"/>
  </default>

  <worldbody>
    <body name="block" pos="0 0 0">
      <freejoint name="root"/>

      <!-- 1.2 x 1.2 x 0.25 m plastic slab, 342 kg -->
      <geom name="block_geom" type="box" size="0.60 0.60 0.125"
            material="plastic" mass="342"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>

  <!-- No actuators - this is a stationary block -->
  <actuator>
  </actuator>
</mujoco>
